## Why This Is Asked

Tests CGO memory ownership, error handling, and thread safety by requiring a C API that allocates memory. The Go binding must copy results and free memory without leaks while goroutines call concurrently.

## Key Concepts

- CGO memory management across Go and C
- Copying C arrays to Go slices safely
- Proper error signaling from C to Go
- Concurrency and independence of buffers

## Code Example

```c
// header
int process_batch(const int* data, size_t n, int** out, size_t* out_len);
```

```c
// implementation
#include <stdlib.h>
int process_batch(const int* data, size_t n, int** out, size_t* out_len) {
  if (!data || n == 0) { *out = NULL; *out_len = 0; return 0; }
  *out_len = n;
  *out = (int*)malloc(n * sizeof(int));
  if (!*out) return -1;
  for (size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) (*out)[i] = data[i] * data[i];
  return 0;
}
```

