## Why This Is Asked
Tests memory ownership across Go and C, preallocated buffers, and error translation. Avoids Go allocations inside C paths and checks thread-safety under concurrency.

## Key Concepts
- CGO memory boundaries and buffer ownership
- Preallocated output buffers and bounds safety
- Error code to Go error mapping
- Concurrency of CGO calls and buffering

## Code Example
```javascript
// Go binding sketch
package tokenb

/*
#include <stdlib.h>
#include "token.h"
*/
import "C"
import (
  "fmt"
  "unsafe"
)

func GenerateToken(prefix string) (string, error) {
  buf := make([]C.char, 256)
  cPrefix := C.CString(prefix)
  defer C.free(unsafe.Pointer(cPrefix))
  var err C.int
  ret := C.generate_token(cPrefix, &buf[0], 256, &err)
  if int(ret) != 0 {
    return "", fmt.Errorf("token error %d", int(err))
  }
  return C.GoString(&buf[0]), nil
}
```

